licence text names no copyright holder; the files are attributed here to the
authors of openai/math (OpenAI).

1. Unmodified upstream files.
   The 44 files under lean/OAI/Computability/FourierCircuit/ are
   byte-for-byte copies of the files with the same paths in openai/math at
   the commit above. They have not been changed. They are the files that the
   proofs of this repository import, directly or indirectly: Core.lean, which
   holds OpenAI's circuit model, and the 43 files that
   TensorCostAlgebra.lean imports other than Core.lean, which hold OpenAI's
   definition of the cost of a matrix and their theorems on the cost of
   tensor products. openai/math has 51 files in that directory; the 7 that
   are not here are Main.lean and the six further files that Main.lean
   needs.
   lean/lean-toolchain is a byte-for-byte copy of lean/lean-toolchain of
   openai/math.
   To check this yourself:

       git clone https://github.com/openai/math openai-math
       git -C openai-math checkout fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb
       for f in $(find lean/OAI -name '*.lean'); do
           cmp "$f" "openai-math/$f" || echo "DIFFERENT $f"; done
       cmp lean/lean-toolchain openai-math/lean/lean-toolchain
       cmp LICENSE openai-math/LICENSE

   The loop and the two commands after it print nothing when the files are
   identical. This was run for these files on 2026-10-11 against a checkout
   of that commit: 44 of 44 identical, and the two other files identical.
   The clone of openai/math takes about 3.2 GB. The commands above put it
   in a folder openai-math/ at the top of this repository; .gitignore
   names that folder, and it can be deleted afterwards.

2. Files that contain upstream text.
   - lean/Work/SmallWHT/ChallengeWHT8.lean contains, as its lines 25-62,
     lines 12-49 of lean/ComparatorChallenges/ExactFourier.lean of
     openai/math (OpenAI's statement of the circuit model), unchanged.
     Everything else in the file was written by the agents of section 4.
   - lean/Work/SmallWHT/TensorPow8.lean contains one theorem of openai/math
     with its proof. Its theorem "exists_circuit_of_cost" (lines 67-81 of
     the file) is the theorem "OAI.ExactFourier.CircuitCost.exists_circuit"
     of lean/OAI/Computability/FourierCircuit/Main.lean (lines 196-210 of
     that file), unchanged except for its name and for spacing. It is
     repeated there so that Main.lean and the six further files that
     Main.lean needs are not included in this repository. The comment above
     the theorem says so. Everything else in the file was written by the
     agents of section 4.
   - lean/lakefile.lean is adapted from lean/lakefile.lean of openai/math:
     the same package name, toolchain, package option and Mathlib pin; every
     other dependency was removed and the three libraries of this repository
     were declared. lean/lake-manifest.json lists Mathlib and its 8
