     openai/math.

3. New files.
   The six files under lean/Work/SmallWHT/, the file
   lean/WHTCheck/Solution.lean, the script lean/tools/Compare.lean and the
   script lean/check.sh are not part of openai/math. The files under
   lean/Work/SmallWHT/ import the upstream files and use their definitions
   and theorems; the header of TensorPow8.lean lists the names it uses.
   lean/WHTCheck/Solution.lean repeats one definition, with three small
   checks of it, from the file of the same name in the repository
   https://github.com/jacobalansussman/wht-power-saving-lean (same author,
   Apache License 2.0); its header gives the line numbers.
   lean/tools/Compare.lean is a byte-for-byte copy of tools/Compare.lean of
   that repository.
   The six files under lean/Work/SmallWHT/ were written inside a working copy
   of that repository and are kept here exactly as they were checked. Where
   their comments say "this repository" or "the repository", they mean
   that one: its function "wht", its main theorems and its earlier
   results. In the comment at the top of lean/tools/Compare.lean, read
   "tools/Compare.lean" for "checks/Compare.lean".
   Everything outside lean/ except LICENSE is new as well, and none of it
   is a file of openai/math: README.md, VERIFY.md, CITATION.cff and this
   file; docs/UNDERSTAND.md and docs/walkthrough.py; the note
   notes/explicit-circuits.md and notes/explicit-circuits.json; the
   programs, circuit texts and recorded outputs under tools/circuits/
   (section 7 says more about two of its folders); the paper with its
   two check programs under paper/; and, added in revision 2 on
   2026-10-22, the folders measurements/2026-10-22/ and tools/fht-kernel/
   (section 8) and the program tools/circuits/count_tables.py with its
   recorded output. The six text files
   under tools/circuits/fast/wht56/circuits/ are byte-for-byte copies of
   files under tools/circuits/programs/. The program
   tools/circuits/lean/slp2lean.py writes Lean source in the circuit model
   of lean/OAI/Computability/FourierCircuit/Core.lean; the comment that
   it writes into that source names paths inside lean/ and says "this
   repository" in the sense just explained, and so do the headers of two
   circuit texts (tools/circuits/programs/README.md names them).

